  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 200 AM Saturday... \n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... Frost/Freeze headlines remain in place this \nmorning, with a Freeze Warning for all of central NC early Sunday \nmorning.\n\nFrost/Freeze headlines have remained unchanged into early this \nmorning. While the aforementioned shortwave and cold front moving \ninto the region early this morning will increase cloud cover, still \nexpect clouds to weaken and disperse through the early morning hours \ntoday. Some light stirring may also inhibit lows from getting below \nfreezing widespread in the Warning area, but given little change in \nguidance with respect to lows, decided to keep frost/freeze \nheadlines intact.\n\nThe more widespread freeze is expected late tonight into Sunday \nmorning. A Continental Polar high of around 1030-mb will settle \nacross the Mid MS valley region. Although not in the most ideal \nposition, the pressure gradient should relax, allowing winds to go \ncalm. Coupled with low-level thicknesses of 1304-1310m, should \nsupport a widespread freeze of mid/upper 20s to low 30s, coldest \nacross the Northern Piedmont. Given the consistent signal in \nguidance, decided to keep the entire area under a Freeze Warning \nSunday morning.",
